      <div class="blog-body">
        <h2>Act in This Order. Do Not Panic.</h2>
        <p>A burst pipe can let out a lot of water very quickly. Every minute you wait means more damage. The steps below are in order. Read them now, so you know what to do if it happens.</p>

        <div class="blog-warning">
          <strong>If you smell gas at any point, stop everything and call Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</strong>
          <p>A gas leak comes before a water leak. Get everyone out. Do not use any switches. Call the gas emergency line before you do anything else. Once the gas is safe, call us on 0151 558 0334.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Step 1: Turn Off the Water at the Stopcock Immediately</h2>
        <p>First, find your stopcock. In most Liverpool homes it is under the kitchen sink. In Victorian terraces it may be in the cellar, under the stairs or near the front door. If you cannot find the one inside, there is often an outside one in the path near your boundary.</p>
        <p>Turn the stopcock clockwise to close it. This stops mains water coming into the house. If it is stuck and will not turn, call us on 0151 558 0334 straight away. Also call <a href="https://www.unitedutilities.com/emergencies/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">United Utilities on 0345 672 3723</a> to ask them to turn off the supply in the street.</p>

        <div class="blog-callout">
          <strong>Find your stopcock now, before an emergency happens</strong>
          <p>Find your stopcock today, while there is no rush. If it has not been used for years, give it a quarter turn to check it moves. A stuck stopcock in an emergency is a real problem. Save its location in your phone so you are not hunting for it at 2am.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Step 2: Turn Off the Hot Water System</h2>
        <p>Next, turn off your boiler and any immersion heater. This stops the boiler firing with no water, which can damage it. It also helps if the burst is on the hot water side.</p>

        <h2>Step 3: Turn On All Cold Taps</h2>
        <p>Open every cold tap in the house. This drains the water left in the pipes, fast. With the stopcock shut, that water goes down the drain, not out of the burst.</p>

        <h2>Step 4: Limit the Damage While You Wait</h2>
        <p>Once the water is off, work on the damage already done:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Move furniture, valuables, electrical items and papers out of the way</li>
          <li>Use towels and buckets to catch drips</li>
          <li>Take photos and short videos of all the damage before you clean up. Your insurer will want them</li>
          <li>If water is near electrics, do not touch anything wet. If it is safe, switch off at the fuse box. Get an electrician to check before you turn the power back on</li>
          <li>Open windows to start drying the room</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Step 5: Call an Emergency Plumber</h2>
        <p>Call us on 0151 558 0334. We are a 24/7 emergency plumber covering all Liverpool postcodes, with a guaranteed 30-minute response. Our Gas Safe registered engineers come out day or night. There is no call-out fee.</p>
        <p>We can talk you through what to do over the phone while you wait.</p>

        <h2>Why Liverpool Properties Are Particularly Vulnerable</h2>
        <p>Liverpool has a lot of Victorian and Edwardian homes. These often have:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Bare pipes in cold lofts or cellar entries</li>
          <li>Very old pipework that is near the end of its life</li>
          <li>Pipes that run through cold spaces, such as garages and back extensions</li>
          <li>Cold water tanks in lofts with no insulation, which can freeze in winter</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Winter is the main season for burst pipes. In a cold snap, homes with bare pipes are at high risk. If you want your pipes checked before winter, call us to book a visit.</p>

        <h2>What to Tell Your Insurer</h2>
        <p>Call your home insurer once the water is under control. We can give you what you need for a claim:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>An itemised invoice for labour and parts</li>
          <li>Photos of the damage and the finished repair</li>
          <li>A written leak report on what caused the burst</li>
          <li>The date and time we came out</li>
        </ul>
        <p>For help with making a claim, Citizens Advice and the Association of British Insurers both give clear, free advice.</p>

        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="pf-faq">
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-red">URGENT</span>&nbsp; Where is the stopcock in a Liverpool Victorian terrace?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>It is usually under the kitchen sink, in the cellar, under the stairs or near the front door. If you cannot find the one inside, there is often an outside one in the path near your boundary. Call us on 0151 558 0334 and we will help you find it over the phone.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does a burst pipe repair cost in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We charge by the hour, with no call-out fee. The first hour is £120 on weekdays from 9am to 4pm. It is £150 in the evening, at night and at weekends, and £180 on bank holidays. All prices include VAT. If the job needs more time, we tell you the price before we carry on.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">INSURANCE</span>&nbsp; Will my home insurance cover a burst pipe repair?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Most home insurance covers water damage from a burst pipe. The repair itself may or may not be covered, so check your policy. We can write a leak report for your claim. Take photos of all the damage before you clean up, and call your insurer once the water is under control.</p></div></details>
          <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you get to me in Liverpool?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We guarantee a 30-minute response across all Liverpool postcodes, 24/7. Call 0151 558 0334 now.</p></div></details>
        </div>
      </div>

